foreign  [Music]  Ty and I'm a YouTube influencer I  suppose a woodworker artist I'm going to  walk you through how I restore a rotting  Christmas sleigh I was involved in a TV  series here in the UK which I got given  the sleigh to restore it was brought in  from Lithuania so the sleigh was pretty  old I'm not too sure exactly how old it  was but it could be 100 years I would  have no idea but it was definitely  pretty old first of all it's covered in  this green like a lime green paint that  somebody's painted I'm not sure if that  was the original color or not it's got  Twisted bars in it the metals all  twisted and battered half the seats  missing on it so there's there's  certainly a lot of work to do  first what I've got to do is unbolt all  of the sleigh the best thing to try and  with this type of restoration is to try  and unbolt everything I can using  different tools because there has been  some different types of nuts and bolts  added to this over the period so I'm  trying different spanners and ratchets  and sockets and things just to try and  get everything unbothered that I can  now I'm going to wire brush the entire  sleigh as well because I just want to  get off all the rust I can uh so it's  probably been on here for years and  years so why brush and everything as  much as possible  so there's like bits of the patterns on  the side there some bits that are  missing in there so I'm going to need to  kind of recreate and reconstruct those  there's an old bit of wood that I can  lose from this to use to cut out the  pieces I'm going to have to chop out a  few of the bits and pieces that I need  from that Old bit of sleigh wood  I'm going to use a jigsaw to cut out the  shapes or the missing parts and then try  and sand it back and glue it in  what I'm gonna have to do to try and  re-create the pattern that's missing on  the other side is just check out the  side that is whole and sort of Trace  that side and then flip it over and then  try and cut out a similar shape to fit  into the missing pattern  now I'm going to have to make a seat for  this sleigh because there isn't one  that's disappeared  so I'm gonna biscuit join the pieces of  wood together to try and make the seat a  whole piece  so when you put the biscuits in I'm  gonna have to put some glue in and get  it all clamped up and leave that  overnight  [Music]  so now with the seat that's now ready  and all glued up I'm gonna have to try  and rough this up a little bit so I'm  going to burn it just try and make it  look a bit old and sort of like in  keeping with the sleigh really because  it's a new piece of wood we've had to  make this seat completely from scratch  so really you're gonna have to burn it  up bang it with a hammer a few times you  know like it's been there for a hundred  years  foreign  the entire sleigh down as much sanding  as possible there's going to be a lot of  hand sanding involved and I'm gonna have  to use a few machines like all the tool  Sanders just to really try and get as  much of this green that someone's  covered this slaying and also with the  metal work as well because it is very  Rusty and it's got some really old paint  on it gonna try and get all that back to  Bare Metal just to try to get off all  the old stuff and preparation really for  the new paint  I want to paint the frame black there's  obviously a few different ways to paint  sleighs but I want a sort of traditional  Santa sleigh and from what I know what  I've grown up to no obvious that the  Santa sleigh is kind of like a bit red  obviously and it's got some black in it  so I'm gonna go with the frame  completely black and then start paying  all the wood A nice bright vibrant Santa  sleigh red  this sleigh is going to need a few coats  of this red because it's going to seep  into the wood quite a bit so we're gonna  need a few coats of the red on it the  black's gonna cover quite well so that's  going to come up alright and I think  with this piece it's going to need hand  painting really because there's so many  individual little areas and little bits  that meet up to the black metal I think  it's just going to be easier to just  hand paint it it's going to take a lot  longer but I think the Finish is going  to be much much better  now I'm gonna have to use a tiny  paintbrush just because it's just a bit  more of a detailed section I want to  make sure I don't get the paint all over  the other paint that I've just put on  there  so I've managed to keep all of the  aluminum that's been put around this  sleigh I'm gonna have to put it all back  in now just basically using some new  Nails just hammering there was really  just making sure it's all banged into  place and it is that type of sort of  aluminum you can just bang it and mold  it around you know the wood and stuff so  it makes it look quite cool anyway  now I'm going to fit everything together  so I'm going to put the new seat in that  I've made get that bolted in and secure  with the backrest on there there's a few  new bolts so I can't have to add into  this because some of them couldn't  really get off before  so that is the sleigh finished the end  story to this is absolutely pretty  amazing because it was part of the show  I obviously had to sell this sleigh and  it's actually was purchased by a chap  who runs a shop in New Zealand so if you  wanted to see this sleigh or actually  take a seat in the sleigh it is now sat  in New Zealand in a shop called the  Christmas Hut  foreign

